==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|disclaimen}}, from {{der|en|xno|disclaimer}}, from {{der|en|fro|desclamer}} ({{cog|fr|déclamer}}), {{m|fro|des-}} + {{m|fro|clamer}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/dɪsˈkleɪm/}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪm|s=2}}
* {{hyph|en|dis|claim}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Mélange a trois-disclaim.wav |Audio (UK)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To completely renounce claims to; to [[deny]] ownership of or responsibility for
#:{{syn|en|disown|disavow|reject}}
#* {{RQ:Dryden Aeneis|book=7|page=424|lines=817–818|text=He calls the Gods to witness their offence, / '''Disclaims''' the War, asserts his Innocence.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1755|author={{w|Hugh Farmer}}|title=Essay on the Demoniacs of the New Testament
|passage=He '''disclaims''' the authority of Jesus.}}
#* {{RQ:Thackeray Pendennis|passage=By heavens if ever you do it again. If ever you dare to show yourself in my house; or give my name at a gambling-house or at any other house, by Jove—at any other house—or give any reference at all to me, or speak to me in the street, by Gad, or any where else until I speak to you—I '''disclaim''' you altogether—I won’t give you another shilling.|volume=II|chapter=V|page=49}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1901|author={{w|W. W. Jacobs}}|title={{w|The Monkey's Paw}}
|passage="I was to say that Maw and Meggins '''disclaim''' all responsibility," continued the other. "They admit no liability at all, but in consideration of your son's services they wish to present you with a certain sum as compensation."}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To deny, as a claim; to [[refuse]].
#* {{RQ:Milman Latin}}
#*: {{quote|en|The payment was irregularly made, if not '''disclaimed'''.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|transitive}} {{lb|en|legal}} To [[relinquish]] or deny having a claim; to [[disavow]] another's claim; to [[decline]] accepting, as an estate, interest, or office.<ref>{{R:Burrell LD}}</ref>
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To make an admission or warning.
#* {{quote-newsgroup|1=en|date=4 December 2000|author=Michael Reuss|title=Clambytes 2000 <Long!>|newsgroup=alt.religion.scientology|url=https://groups.google.com/g/alt.religion.scientology/c/AmCKUJDzVdk/|text=I '''disclaim''' that there will be a lot of inside humor. If you don't read a.r.s often, or are a newbie, you won't get some of the gags.}}

